---
// The headline feature. The argument is arithmetic, so the numbers carry it: a
// real table, tabular figures, and the one row that is the panel's actual mode
// marked as the answer rather than described as one.
interface Props {
  /** the home page links out; /gamescale is the destination */
  compact?: boolean;
}

const { compact = false } = Astro.props;

const LAUNCH_OPTION = 'gamescale %command%';

const MODES = [
  { what: 'The panel itself', res: '2560×1600', cost: 'what the hardware has' },
  { what: 'XWayland, scale factor 1', res: '1920×1200', cost: 'upscaled to fit; soft' },
  { what: 'XWayland, scale factor 2', res: '3840×2400', cost: '2.25× the pixels, same image' },
];
---

<div class="gs">
  <div class="gs-copy">
    <p class="gs-deck">
      Run a game at&nbsp;1&times; so XWayland hands it the panel&rsquo;s real mode, then put the
      desktop back when it&nbsp;exits.
    </p>
    <p class="lede">
      Under GNOME fractional scaling, XWayland is handed an integer multiple of your{' '}
      <em>logical</em>{' '}
      resolution, never the panel&rsquo;s real&nbsp;mode. At 133% on a 2560&times;1600 display no
      factor lands on the hardware, and a borderless-fullscreen game takes whatever the
      desktop&nbsp;reports.
    </p>

    <table class="modes">
      <caption class="sr-only">Resolution reported to an XWayland game at each scale factor</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">What the game is handed</th>
          <th scope="col">Resolution</th>
          <th scope="col">Cost</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          MODES.map((mode) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{mode.what}</th>
              <td class="res">{mode.res}</td>
              <td class="verdict">{mode.cost}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
        <tr class="is-native">
          <th scope="row">With <strong>gamescale</strong></th>
          <td class="res">2560&times;1600</td>
          <td class="verdict">the panel&rsquo;s real mode</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="gs-side">
    <arc-code-block
      class="theme-fixed-dark"
     
      language="bash"
      filename="steam"
      code={LAUNCH_OPTION}
    ></arc-code-block>
    <p>
      Scale goes to 1.0 for the lifetime of that one process, font and cursor sizes are compensated
      so the desktop stays usable, and everything goes back when the game&nbsp;exits.
    </p>
    <p>
      Including when it doesn&rsquo;t exit cleanly: a watchdog, a state file on disk, and a login
      reconcile unit mean a crash or a <code>SIGKILL</code> still gives you your desktop&nbsp;back.
    </p>
    {
      compact ? (
        <arc-button href="/gamescale" variant="secondary">How gamescale works</arc-button>
      ) : (
        <p class="hint">
          The script, its top-bar indicator, and the reconcile unit ship in the image at a
          pinned&nbsp;tag. Flatpak launchers need one grant from{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/arclight-digital/gamescale">gamescale&rsquo;s installer</a>:
          Flatpak reserves <code>/usr</code>, so no image can hand them a host&nbsp;binary.
        </p>
      )
    }
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .gs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .gs-deck {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--font-display-weight);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    line-height: var(--heading-lh);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    text-wrap: balance;
    max-width: 30ch;
  }

  .modes {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }
  .modes th,
  .modes td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md) var(--space-sm) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    vertical-align: baseline;
  }
  .modes thead th {
    border-top: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-label);
    font-weight: var(--label-weight);
    font-size: var(--label-inline-size);
    letter-spacing: var(--label-spacing);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .modes tbody th {
    font-weight: var(--body-weight);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .res {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .verdict {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  /* the answer: lifted to primary, then to the accent -- ARC's hierarchy rule */
  .is-native th,
  .is-native td {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    border-top-color: var(--border-bright);
  }
  .is-native .res {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    text-shadow: var(--glow-xs);
  }
  .is-native .verdict {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .gs-side arc-code-block {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  @media (max-width: 56rem) {
    .gs {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
